"rationale": "The pedestrian is crossing the ego vehicle's path at x=18.8m with a lateral velocity of 1.2 m/s. Given the ego vehicle's initial speed of 50 kph (~13.9 m/s), the time to reach the conflict point is approximately 1.35 seconds. The pedestrian will have moved from y=-4.0m to approximately y=-2.4m by that time, which is still within the drivable area (y >= -1.75m is the boundary, but the pedestrian is approaching it). More critically, the pedestrian is actively crossing into the lane. A moderate deceleration (A2) is required to ensure the ego vehicle arrives at the conflict point after the pedestrian has cleared the lane or to maintain a safe following distance, as stopping completely (A0/A1) might be excessive if the pedestrian clears quickly, but maintaining speed (A3/A4) is unsafe. A2 provides a safe buffer."
